{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>Take heed because of him, etc.</b> Here He commanded positive commandments and negative commandments. Corresponding to the negative commandments He said <b>take heed</b>, etc., for every instance of \"take heed,\" etc., is a negative commandment. And corresponding to the positive commandments He said <b>and hearken to his voice</b>." "<b>Do not rebel against him.</b> Here is an allusion to the conduct of a person whereby a transformation of good into evil is brought about — \"and a servant ruling, and a maidservant inheriting her mistress\" (Proverbs 30:23). And through this, vengeance will be exacted from the one who effects the transformation, and <b>he will not pardon your transgression</b>. This angel too is known, for he is the aspect of strict justice, and he bears no sin, as it says <b>for he will not pardon</b>, etc. And His saying <b>for My name is within him</b> — understand this matter, for through the intermediary of a person's sin, the departure of the Ally from his midst is brought about. And I will give you insight: Metatron the holy one — the Sages, may their memory be for blessing, said (Sanhedrin 38b) — his name is like the name of his Master, namely Shaddai, for it yields the numerical value of the Name itself. And through a person's sin, the name Shaddai departs from him. This is the sod of the verse (Isaiah 19:5): ״וְנָהָר יֶחֱרַב״, etc. And an understanding heart will understand these matters from His saying <b>for if you truly hearken to his voice</b> — as though speaking of someone other than Himself. And He concluded by saying <b>and you will do all that I speak</b>, and did not say \"that he speaks\" — to say that <b>My name is within him</b>. Understand this."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:33:01.954032151Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}